    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Sample Descriptive Statistics\"\nformat: html\n---\n\n\nIn this file, we'll import all of the Dallas County files provided and create preliminary cross-tabulations and merges to explore basic counts, trends, and double check primary keys and joins across the data files. \n\nSee `Codebooks` and `Data Diagram` tabs for more information on each individual data file. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<br>\n\n# Sample Descriptives\n\n**Data Sample:** Supervision records of DCJD juveniles on either Court-Ordered Probation/Permanent Probation/Deferred Prosecution at any point from 10/1/2017 through 9/30/2022\n\n\n\n## Table 1. Unique Youth and Referrals by Year (Year of Referral)\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-striped table-hover table-condensed table-responsive\" style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Year of Referral </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Unique Youth (N) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Unique Referrals (N) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Referrals, Percent of Sample (%) </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2010 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.0% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2011 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 9 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 12 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.1% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2012 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 32 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 38 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.2% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2013 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 90 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 121 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.6% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2014 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 281 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 431 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2.2% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2015 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 590 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1,000 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 5.0% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2016 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1,210 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2,045 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 10.2% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2017 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2,286 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 3,556 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 17.8% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2018 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2,491 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 3,742 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 18.8% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2019 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2,424 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 3,609 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 18.1% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2020 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1,479 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2,029 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 10.2% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2021 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1,456 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1,969 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 9.9% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2022 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 992 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1,400 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 7.0% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> Overall </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> 7,661 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> 19,953 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> 100.0% </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\n<br><br>\n\n## Join 1. Join of `Child` and `Offenses`\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\n### left join of child file to offenses file in order to see if there is much missingness\n### i.e. are there offenses without demo records? \noffenses_child_demo_join <- \n  left_join(offenses_clean,\n            child_clean,\n            by = \"unique_id\") ### join looks good; all records join\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n```\nleft_join: added 9 columns (birth_date, gender, race, ethnicity, mental_health_needs, …)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n```\n           > rows only in x        0\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n```\n           > rows only in y  (     0)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n```\n           > matched rows     28,567\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n```\n           >                 ========\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stderr}\n```\n           > rows total       28,567\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n## Table 2: Unique Youth and Referrals by Race/Ethnicity\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-striped table-hover table-condensed table-responsive\" style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Race/Ethnicity </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Unique Youth (N) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Unique Youth, Percent of Sample (%) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Unique Referrals (N) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Referrals, Percent of Sample (%) </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> Asian </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 74 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1.0% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 120 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.6% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> Black </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 3,379 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 44.1% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 9,528 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 47.8% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> Hispanic </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 3,443 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 44.9% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 8,734 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 43.8% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> White </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 757 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 9.9% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 1,548 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 7.8% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> Other </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 8 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.1% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 23 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.1% </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> Overall </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> 7,661 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> 100.0% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> 19,953 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> 100.0% </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n## Table 3: Average Offenses per Referral over Time\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-striped table-hover table-condensed table-responsive\" style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text